diff --git a/internal/agentwire/reliability.go b/internal/agentwire/reliability.go
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..91c2ab1
--- /dev/null
+++ b/internal/agentwire/reliability.go
@@ -0,0 +1,51 @@
+//go:build !no_mcp
+
+package agentwire
+
+const reliabilityMarkdown = `# Execution reliability
+
+Ordinary files and images are verified and written before an exec backend starts.
+The node retries input reads, not model execution. Missing, corrupt or over-limit
+inputs fail the attempt explicitly. The current input limit is 16 files and 32 MiB
+total per retained conversation. A chat-completions backend has no local filesystem
+and explicitly refuses ordinary files; use an exec backend for file work.
+
+An operator can configure one authorized root with:
+
+    anet autoreply set --backend exec --agent <agent> --work-dir <absolute-root> --workspace-mode managed
+
+Supported exec agents are cursor, claude, codex, opencode, openclaw and hermes.
+The configured agent selects an existing project or a new project on the first
+turn. The node validates the selection, stores a task binding and holds a root
+lock during execution. Later turns reuse the binding. Existing projects need a
+projects/<slug>/project.json catalog entry; this does not auto-import arbitrary
+directories. A remote path cannot authorize a new root. This routing mode does
+not add a sandbox or desktop permission; existing backend policies still apply.
+
+Task metadata anet.execution includes the attempt_id, instruction_revision,
+phase, heartbeat_at, last_progress_at, last_output_at, process_state, side_effects,
+error_category, error_summary and exit_code when known. Heartbeat means the
+supervisor is alive. Output means bytes arrived. Neither proves business progress.
+Unobservable tool/model blocking remains unknown rather than being guessed.
+anet.execution_attempts preserves each attempt with its phase timeline; log_ref
+locates private event JSON files under the autoreply module's state directory.
+
+anet.instruction distinguishes queued, delivered_to_executor and
+next_turn_pending_stop. New messages stop the previous execution before another
+turn starts; hot steering is not assumed. A transactional revision check refuses
+old replies. Results name the exact instruction revision. Canceling an A2A task
+is not proof of process termination: anet.execution_stop may remain unconfirmed.
+Do not retry work with possible side effects merely because cancellation returned.
+
+Backend failures are failed with anet.reason=backend_failed. They are not user
+questions. A2A terminal tasks remain terminal: after inspecting effects, recovery
+uses a new task in the same context. The failed task and its evidence remain
+queryable. A locally interrupted attempt is not automatically executed again.
+Runner stop confirmation requires this build at both node and runner.
+
+Receipt verification and business verification are distinct. Ordinary text work
+reports anet.business_verification=not_automatically_verified. Skill effect_status
+keeps its existing semantics. Outbox evidence contains node-computed file digests.
+An optional anet-evidence.json can report tests/screenshots/checks and their scope;
+these claims are marked reported_by_backend, never independent verification.
+`
